# Scheduled jobs for the-invisible-cities.com, as defined in Forge's Scheduler (user: forge).
# Documentation only — nothing installs this file. Forge's scheduler did not show up in
# `crontab -l` for forge or root on the droplet (checked 2026-10-23), so Forge runs these some
# other way; leaving Forge means adding them to the forge user's crontab (`crontab -e`).

# kirby cache cleanup — empties Kirby's generated page-media cache on the volume (Forge "weekly")
# The static page cache (site/cache/<host>/pages) holds HTML that points at those thumbnails, and
# Kirby can only regenerate a thumbnail from its .jobs/*.json file, which the wipe also deletes. So
# the page cache MUST be cleared in the same job, otherwise cached pages 404 their images until
# the next deploy/Panel edit. Order matters: media first, then pages.
@weekly rm -rf /mnt/data-volume/media/pages/* /home/forge/the-invisible-cities.com/current/site/cache/the-invisible-cities.com/pages
